    Bug 1914180 - Make Maildir folder parsing resilient against inaccessible files. r=BenC


    Previously, `MaildirScanner::NextFile()` would abort the entire folder scan
    if it failed to open a single file (e.g., due to an antivirus lock, or
    encountering a subdirectory). This starved the MSF index of remaining messages,
    causing them to disappear from the UI while remaining visible on disk.

    This patch fixes the fragility by:
    * Introducing a loop with explicit sanity checks to safely bypass inaccessible
      or invalid files, allowing the scan to continue without causing recursive
      stack overflows.
    * Reordering stream initialization to occur *before* `OnStartMessage()` is
      fired. This ensures we only promise the listener a message if we have
      successfully acquired a valid file handle, preventing dangling listener
      states.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D296984

